id: pm-gh1535
title: "GH-1535: report context test health over the matching population"
description: "Reproduce GH-1535: tests counters use the focus page while summary uses matching_items. Compute test health over the same filtered active population independently of focus limits. Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1535"
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-21T16:30:10.816Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T18:35:44.116Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-21T18:35:42.533Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-21T18:35:42.533Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: Test counters are invariant under focus limits; Filters and active statuses constrain the denominator; Public SDK and human output declare test scope and denominator
parent: pm-gh1361
risk: medium
confidence: 90
resolution: Count all matching active items; expose scope and denominator; cap Markdown failure identities by focus amount and token cost with omitted counts.
expected_result: "Exact counters across focus limits and bounded failure details through SDK, CLI and MCP; strict canonical coverage remains required."
actual_result: "All48 linked context cases pass including direct SDK row-cap proof, CLI transport rendering, the tiny token ceiling, and complete structured counters. Hosted full-source coverage and static quality remain merge prerequisites."
